# What a model directory accumulates, and none of it belongs in the history.
#
# This file decides what gets PUBLISHED: a version is a commit, and a draft
# (`hammerola build`) is the working copy with what git ignores left out. A file
# the model reads, or a document `project.json` names, has to be committed.
# `git status --ignored` lists what will not be published.

# Bytecode, from any local run of the model.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Exported geometry, in case something writes it beside the source. The hub
# exports into its own directory and hands the files back over HTTP; a mesh at
# the root of a model repository is a stray. Only at the root: a reference
# mesh committed under `ref/` is published with the model.
/*.stl
/*.step
/*.stp
/*.3mf

# The local environment, and the one file that may hold the hub's secret.
# `.env` stays out of every commit, so out of every push -- the token travels in
# one HTTP header and nowhere else.
.venv/
.env

# `.hammerola/` -- what `hammerola artifacts` and `comments files` fetch -- is
# NOT listed here on purpose: the tool writes a `.gitignore` of its own inside
# that directory the first time it creates it, so it is already covered from
# the inside and stays covered if the name ever changes.
